=46rom: "Kirill A. Shutemov" <kirill.shutemov@linux.intel.com>
Subject: page-flags: define PG_locked behavior on compound pages

lock_page() must operate on the whole compound page.  It doesn't make m=
uch
sense to lock part of compound page.  Change code to use head page's
PG_locked, if tail page is passed.

This patch also gets rid of custom helper functions -- __set_page_locke=
d()
and __clear_page_locked().  They are replaced with helpers generated by
__SETPAGEFLAG/__CLEARPAGEFLAG.  Tail pages to these helper would trigge=
r
VM_BUG_ON().

SLUB uses PG_locked as a bit spin locked.  IIUC, tail pages should neve=
r
appear there.  VM_BUG_ON() is added to make sure that this assumption i=
s
correct.

[akpm@linux-foundation.org: fix fs/cifs/file.c]
